# AGENTS.md — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

The repository entry point for agents that read `AGENTS.md` (Codex, among
others), the way Claude reads `CLAUDE.md`. It states the contract every session
runs under and links the files where the full doctrine lives — it binds that
doctrine into this runtime; it does not fork it.

## Where the contract lives

- **The living plan is [`{{HANDOFF_PATH}}`]({{HANDOFF_PATH}}).** Read it at
  session start; update it at wrap-up. It — not an agent's memory, not a
  scratch note — is the single source of truth for what is done, in progress,
  and next. The session bookends are skills: `session-start` to pick up work,
  `wrap-up` to hand it off.
- **Everything project-specific lives in `config/dev-model.yaml`.** Skills and
  engines read it from there; never hardcode a value that belongs in it.
- **Read the shared contract before changing anything, then the nearest
  path-scoped rule.** Behavioral changes to `{{ENGINE_DIR}}/pr_watch.py`,
  `{{ENGINE_DIR}}/dev_session.sh`, `{{ENGINE_DIR}}/launch_lane.py`, or the profile
  named by `parallel.claude_settings_profile` (shipped as
  `config/claude-lane-settings.json`),
  along with customer-facing send paths,
  destructive operations, and kill/recovery paths, are governed by
  [`docs/agentic-dev-kit/safety-critical-changes.md`](docs/agentic-dev-kit/safety-critical-changes.md);
  when the configured review bot cannot review, the substitute is the panel in
  [`docs/agentic-dev-kit/fallback-review-panel.md`](docs/agentic-dev-kit/fallback-review-panel.md).
- Tracker board: {{TRACKER_URL}}

## Branches and pull requests

- `{{PROTECTED_BRANCH}}` is protected — never commit to it directly. Branch and
  open a PR.
- **Open completed work ready for review by default.** Ready status invites review;
  it does not authorize merge. Draft is only for the bounded exception where a
  material unfinished-work window must already exist on the remote pull request,
  such as required forge-hosted validation that cannot run before the PR exists.
  The run that opens a draft owns the ready transition as soon as the work and body
  are complete; risk, broad scope, human review, and operator-held merge authority
  are not draft reasons by themselves. Run `pr-watch --assert-ready` after ready
  creation or transition, before review polling. The executable lifecycle is in
  [`docs/agentic-dev-kit/workflows/pr-watch.md`](docs/agentic-dev-kit/workflows/pr-watch.md).
- **Opening or pushing a PR is not completion: follow it through CI and
  review.** The `pr-watch` skill is that loop — poll, fix, acknowledge,
  re-poll — until the PR is green and every review finding is fixed or
  explicitly answered.
- **Require an independent review pass before any authorized self-merge. A
  missing, skipped, or rate-limited review is not a clean review** — a green
  check whose description says the reviewer was rate-limited reviewed nothing.

## Verification

- The verification command is `<name it here — the one command that runs this
  repo's whole suite, so no session has to rediscover it>`. Run it as its own
  step and read its result before committing anything; a compound chain that
  ends in a push hides the failure exactly when it matters.
- **Do not infer that a successful process exit means a deliverable exists.**
  Look at the artifact.
- **Prefer deterministic validation and receipts over prompt-only assurances.**
  When you claim something is verified, name the command that established it
  and its actual result.

## Devkit boundary

- **Do not hand-edit kit-owned files.** `{{ENGINE_DIR}}/kit_doctor.py` reports
  which shipped files have drifted; anything project-specific belongs in
  `config/dev-model.yaml`, not inside an engine.
- Reusable workflow behaviour is ported **upstream** to the kit, not grown in a
  local fork of an engine or skill.
- **Keep Claude/Codex differences in thin runtime adapters; do not fork the
  workflow semantics.** The runtime-neutral definitions live in
  `docs/agentic-dev-kit/workflows/`; `.claude/commands/` and `.agents/skills/`
  are bindings over them, and so is this file.

## Yours to extend

The sections above are the generic spine. What only this repo knows belongs
below — add it here, keep it current at wrap-up. Ready-made material is in
